# AGENTS.kotlin.md — Kotlin (any target)

Additive to `../AGENTS.md`. Applies to every `.kt` / `.kts` file: Android, KMP,
Spring Boot, CLIs and libraries. Target rules are in `AGENTS.android.md`,
`AGENTS.kmp.md` and `AGENTS.spring.md`.

## Build and check

```bash
./gradlew ktlintFormat                      # fix formatting first
./gradlew ktlintCheck detekt                # must pass
./gradlew test                              # JVM modules; Android variants: see AGENTS.android.md
```

Never commit with `ktlintCheck` failing "because CI will format it". CI does not
format. CI fails.

## Kotlin rules

- No `!!`. If you believe a value cannot be null, encode that in the type or use
  `requireNotNull(x) { "why this cannot be null" }` with a real message. detekt
  enforces this; the pre-commit hook accepts `// allow-bang` on a line it must
  let through.
- No `runBlocking` outside tests and `main()`. Suspend functions all the way up.
  The one in `main()` gets a `// allow-blocking` comment so CI stays quiet.
- No `GlobalScope`. Use the injected scope (on Android, `viewModelScope`).
- Dispatchers are injected, never hardcoded: take a `CoroutineDispatcher`
  parameter (or a `DispatcherProvider`) so tests can substitute.
- Never swallow `CancellationException`. A `catch (e: Exception)` or
  `runCatching` around a suspend call must rethrow it.
- Prefer `sealed interface` for state, `data class` for payloads, `value class`
  for identifiers. A `String` userId is a bug waiting to be swapped with a
  `String` sessionId.
- Public API of a module needs KDoc on the entry points only. Do not KDoc
  private functions to satisfy a linter.
- No new `object` singletons holding mutable state. Use DI.

## Gradle rules

- Dependencies are declared in `gradle/libs.versions.toml` only. No inline
  `implementation("group:artifact:1.2.3")` in a module build file.
- No new Gradle plugin without Platform review. Plugins are Kitchen.
- Module build files stay boring: plugins block, the target's block (`android`,
  `kotlin`, `springBoot`), dependencies. Custom logic goes in a convention plugin
  under `build-logic/`.

## Testing

- Unit tests for logic, Turbine for flows, `runTest` for coroutines (never
  `Thread.sleep` or real delays).
- A bug fix lands with a test that fails before the fix. No exceptions, and this
  is the one rule an agent may not "simplify".
- Do not delete or `@Ignore` a failing test to make CI green. Quarantining is a
  human decision, recorded in the PR.

